←: ## Summary Both bugs trace to `js/file-folder.js`'s shared `FileFolder` mechanism (used by `MidiFolder`/`LifeFolder` alike), not to anything Life-specific. The Life "Save As" wiring itself is correct and properly implemented — the actual defect is a permission-mode bug in the shared write path, and the shared listing mechanism is a cached snapshot by design with no re-list-on-open behavior. ### 1. Life's Save As implementation — properly wired, but write path silently fails `[REDACTED_PRIVATE_INFO]` — `<button id="life-save" ...>` `[REDACTED_PERSON]` — `bind('life-save', this.save);` `[REDACTED_PERSON]` — `LifeMode.save`: ```js save: async function() { ... if (typeof LifeFolder !== 'undefined') { await LifeFolder.saveFileAs(filename, text); // downloads as a plain blob if no folder is set return; } ... } ``` This correctly calls into the shared `saveFileAs` — Life is NOT missing the folder-write capability; it's wired identically to Compose's `MidiFolder.saveFileAs` (`[REDACTED_PERSON]`). The …[7352 chars elided]… ndle that has read-but-not-write permission, which is exactly the real-world state `showDirectoryPicker()`'s default `mode: 'read'` produces. - No mention anywhere in `docs/invariants.md` or `next_steps.md` of "listing is a one-time snapshot" or "no live refresh" being a deliberate, documented scope limit for the local-folder tier; `next_steps.md:9` just documents the original MidiFolder feature landing, with no caveat about staleness. **Conclusion:** both bugs are real, fixable defects in `js/file-folder.js`, not documented/intended limitations: - Bug 1: `saveFileAs`/`chooseFolder`/`restore`/`reconnect` only ever deal in `'read'` permission, never `'readwrite'`, so the folder-write branch throws and silently falls back to download. - Bug 2: `fileHandles`/dropdown listing is refreshed only at four explicit trigger points (setup/restore, reconnect, choose-folder, post-save), never on dropdown open, so external OS-level file moves aren't picked up until one of those triggers fires again.


