Committed as `[REDACTED_SECRET]`. Summary of what shipped:

**Life mode:**
- Automaton source dropdown now has an "Upload File…" menu item (scoped to Life only, via a new `hasUpload` flag on the shared `FileFolder`), replacing the separate button that vanished entirely on Chrome.
- A plain download link (⬇) always serves the *current* board as `.yaml`, no filename prompt — distinct from Save As.
- Current rule (Survival/Birth, or state count + order for multi-state automata) now shows under the generation counter.

**Melody mode:** the "3 clean reps" measure-jump was already correctly gated, but a separate unconditional timeout was growing the drilled segment by one note after every single clean pass regardless — so in practice advancement always felt like it took 1 rep. Fixed so song mode only advances via that same 3-rep gate; Random is untouched.

All new/existing tests pass (155 desktop, node unit tests, INV-13).

